# Files outside base/base-v1 and base/base-v2 that may import com.amazonaws, software.amazon.awssdk, or
# software.amazon.dax. checkModuleBoundaries (project/ModuleBoundaryCheck.scala) enforces this list.
#
# Write each entry as `<path>  # <reason>`. An entry without a reason fails.
# Files in base/base-v1 and base/base-v2 import the SDK without an entry, and an entry for them fails.
# A new entry is allowed only in a module that already holds SDK imports (ModuleBoundaryCheck.Modules), and the PR
# that adds it gives the same reason. A core module such as base/base or journal-base cannot import the SDK at all.
# An entry whose file no longer imports the SDK fails, so the list shrinks when an import goes away.

example/src/test/scala/com/github/j5ik2o/pekko/persistence/dynamodb/example/untyped/eventsourced/CounterSpec.scala  # BaseCounterSpec queries the journal rows with the v1 QueryRequest to assert what was written.
journal/journal-v1/src/main/scala/com/github/j5ik2o/pekko/persistence/dynamodb/journal/dao/v1/V1JournalRowReadDriver.scala  # Deprecated v1 facade whose public constructor takes the v1 AmazonDynamoDB clients.
